# Datasets are never committed. The Google+ download unpacks as a directory
# named gplus_combined.txt holding a 1.3 GB file of the same name; the HepTh
# one carries ~29,000 abstract files beside the edge list. Both are documented
# in data/README.md with the URL to fetch them from.
data/cit-HepTH/
gplus_combined.txt/
*.edgelist
Graph Deanonymization2024/

# The data/ edge lists are tracked on purpose. Without this exception the
# blanket *.edgelist rule above would silently drop anything added there.
!data/**/*.edgelist

# Generated evaluation pairs and experiment outputs. Regenerable from a parent
# graph plus a seed, so only the generator is tracked -- see
# src/beta_noise_generator/. data/ is for source datasets only.
runs/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Generated run outputs. Only the Dec 2024 submissions are kept, in
# results/archive_2024/; everything else in results/ is regenerable.
results/*
!results/archive_2024/

# Run records are the exception to that rule, and tracked on purpose. A record
# describes a run in an environment that no longer exists -- a torch nightly, a
# dirty tree, a GPU -- so unlike the bytes it describes it cannot be
# regenerated. The bytes stay in runs/ with their digests held here. See
# docs/experiment_logging_policy.md.
!results/runs/

# Large or binary artifacts do not belong in a record directory even so; the
# record carries their SHA-256 instead.
results/runs/**/*.npz
results/runs/**/*.edgelist

# Rendered proposal output
docs/proposal.pdf
proposal.pdf

# Local-only working files. These stay on disk and Claude Code still reads
# them; git ignoring a file does not hide it from the filesystem.
CLAUDE.md
SeedFree_Li.etal.pdf

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
